1
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:49,959
Well,

2
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,480
I wanted to let you know...

3
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,120
the ledger,

4
00:01:52,879 --> 00:01:53,879
I gave it to my brother and the others.

5
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,799
H-How are you gonna explain this to your dad?

6
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:59,400
Let my brother explain it.

7
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:00,680
They barged right to my door.

8
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,000
I had no choice but to hand it over.

9
00:02:03,159 --> 00:02:03,959
Even taking a step back,

10
00:02:04,439 --> 00:02:06,640
even if that ledger were still in my hands,

11
00:02:06,879 --> 00:02:08,240
if it were up to me,

12
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:11,319
I'd agree with Ma Laibu.

13
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,080
Cash out.

14
00:02:19,599 --> 00:02:20,039
Uncle Ma,

15
00:02:20,759 --> 00:02:21,560
this hurdle right now...

16
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:22,840
is really hard to get over.

17
00:02:23,439 --> 00:02:24,919
If the phase three payment doesn't come through,

18
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,599
our accounts will be completely drained.

19
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,159
What about yours?

20
00:02:29,719 --> 00:02:31,800
W-We're pretty much the same.

21
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,439
But luckily,

22
00:02:34,879 --> 00:02:36,199
as for veterans like Biaozi,

23
00:02:36,719 --> 00:02:38,039
if I step in and talk to them,

24
00:02:38,319 --> 00:02:39,680
we can still hold out a bit longer.

25
00:02:40,039 --> 00:02:41,039
Hold out until when?

26
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,120
How much longer can you hold out?

27
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:44,159
What if Tengyue just refuses to pay?

28
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,240
Uncle Ma,

29
00:02:47,039 --> 00:02:49,120
there are only two options in front of us now.

30
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:50,439
One,

31
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:51,919
just like you said:

32
00:02:52,199 --> 00:02:52,840
tough it out.

33
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,280
Hold out till whenever you can,

34
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,000
take it day by day.

35
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:55,800
Hang on for as long as possible,

36
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,400
however long that is.

37
00:02:56,719 --> 00:02:57,280
But in the end?

38
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,400
It'll kill us!

39
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,080
The little guy can't fight a giant.

40
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,560
The other path:

41
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:04,319
terminate the contract cleanly,

42
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,159
and walk away happy.

43
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,080
Look,

44
00:03:07,639 --> 00:03:10,479
aren't I still handling legal affairs at Tengyue?

45
00:03:10,719 --> 00:03:11,560
I still have some sway.

46
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:12,639
Maybe...

47
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,120
we can even get a bit more.

48
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,240
Can't we just quit this job and walk?

49
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:18,800
What... what does your dad think?

50
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,199
Isn't he still bedridden in the hospital?

51
00:03:23,439 --> 00:03:24,360
I couldn't bring it up to him.

52
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,319
But I've talked it over with Uncle Wei.

53
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:27,599
We see eye to eye.

54
00:03:28,039 --> 00:03:29,360
We both think it won't be long.

55
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:31,840
Uncle Ma,

56
00:03:32,639 --> 00:03:35,439
a mom-and-pop construction crew like ours...

57
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:36,400
can't weather these storms.

58
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:37,840
I'm not trying to scare you.

59
00:03:38,919 --> 00:03:39,800
Right now,

60
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:41,400
if we don't get out,

61
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,199
and we keep waiting...

62
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,639
it'll be too late to run.

63
00:03:45,319 --> 00:03:46,199
Think it over.

64
00:03:56,719 --> 00:03:57,159
Xiuliang.

65
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,599
I'll ask you one last time.

66
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,960
What if the three of us

67
00:04:02,199 --> 00:04:03,199
insist on merging?

68
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,199
Will you help us or not?

69
00:04:05,199 --> 00:04:06,719
No. I'm definitely staying out of it.

70
00:04:07,319 --> 00:04:08,800
Uncle Ma, even if I stepped in,

71
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,280
it'd still be a dead end.

72
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,080
Uncle Ma...

73
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,520
Worked hard all our lives,

74
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,839
and just like that, it's over.

75
00:04:19,199 --> 00:04:20,079
Brother-in-law.

76
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,959
There's really nothing to be sad about.

77
00:04:22,399 --> 00:04:23,839
Friends are friends,

78
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:25,079
but business is business.

79
00:04:25,279 --> 00:04:26,000
When it comes to money,

80
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,720
it only counts once it's in your pocket.

81
00:04:28,959 --> 00:04:30,560
You can't wait until the crew

82
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,839
completely rots in your hands

83
00:04:31,839 --> 00:04:32,600
before you start having regrets.

84
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,000
By then, it'll be too late.

85
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:37,319
What kind of life is this?

86
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:38,680
I... What am I...

87
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,680
Let me take a moment of your morning meeting

88
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:04,519
to introduce

89
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,600
our new director of cardiac surgery,

90
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:08,360
Director Lin Hong.

91
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,839
Thank you, President Qian Hao.

92
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,279
And thank you, colleagues.

93
00:05:17,959 --> 00:05:19,879
I'm glad to be working with all of you.

94
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,800
I know cardiac surgery has always been

95
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,199
a key department in our hospital,

96
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,160
with an impressive track record.

97
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,600
I also hope to work with everyone

98
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:28,560
to make our department even better.

99
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:30,240
In particular,

100
00:05:30,519 --> 00:05:31,360
to be able to learn from

101
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,199
so many outstanding seniors.

102
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:34,120
And of course,

103
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,480
Director Jin here.

104
00:05:35,759 --> 00:05:38,439
I heard you've worked here for over a decade

105
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,639
and have a wealth of experience.

106
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:41,680
I hope you'll guide me along the way.

107
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,199
Director Lin, you're too kind.

108
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,040
We'll learn from each other.

109
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,199
Today,

110
00:05:45,319 --> 00:05:46,680
on behalf of the entire department,

111
00:05:47,079 --> 00:05:48,399
if, in your work down the road,

112
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,319
you ever need anything,

113
00:05:49,439 --> 00:05:49,959
just say the word.

114
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:51,199
We'll give our full cooperation

115
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,279
and support you.

116
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,120
Thank you.

117
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:53,639
All right.

118
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,040
Let's all get back to work.

119
00:05:55,879 --> 00:05:56,319
Director Lin,

120
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,199
let me show you your office.

121
00:05:58,319 --> 00:05:58,600
Okay.

122
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:08,759
Let's grab a bite.

123
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,639
He's in a bad mood today.

124
00:06:15,199 --> 00:06:16,040
When you talk to him,

125
00:06:16,319 --> 00:06:16,680
watch what you say.

126
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:17,920
Don't worry.

127
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,199
I know what I'm doing.

128
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,319
Let me tell you,

129
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,759
the new director is younger than him.

130
00:06:22,959 --> 00:06:24,319
If he wants to climb any higher,

131
00:06:24,959 --> 00:06:25,399
it'll be tough.

132
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,480
That guy came from Beijing,

133
00:06:27,959 --> 00:06:28,839
so he'll have to head back eventually.

134
00:06:29,759 --> 00:06:30,959
Director Jin's name,

135
00:06:31,319 --> 00:06:32,439
in a place like Honggang,

136
00:06:32,639 --> 00:06:33,319
still carries weight.

137
00:06:33,959 --> 00:06:35,319
Lao Jin is the one I trust most.

138
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,800
Anyway, this is a real chance.

139
00:06:38,519 --> 00:06:39,399
When you have time,

140
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,800
put in a good word for me.

141
00:06:41,199 --> 00:06:41,839
Everything you've done for me,

142
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:44,040
I'll always remember it.

143
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,560
Got it.

144
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:46,600
Keep it down.

145
00:06:48,759 --> 00:06:49,199
He's here.

146
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:49,920
Director Jin.

147
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:53,319
Director Jin.

148
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:54,800
Since you're already here,

149
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:55,920
have a bite before you go.

150
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:56,879
I know what you're thinking.

151
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,600
I can't help you.

152
00:06:58,079 --> 00:06:59,759
You're already here. Have a seat first.

153
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:00,600
I'm just a deputy.

154
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,519
I really can't help you.

155
00:07:01,519 --> 00:07:02,519
Chief or deputy, what does it matter?

156
00:07:02,519 --> 00:07:03,600
Everyone's gotta eat.

157
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,199
Come on.

158
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,639
Sit down, please.

159
00:07:06,199 --> 00:07:06,720
Have a seat.

160
00:07:08,319 --> 00:07:08,720
Brother,

161
00:07:09,079 --> 00:07:10,360
chief or deputy doesn't mean a thing.

162
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,800
In my eyes, you're the best in all of Honggang.

163
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,480
In all of Honggang,

164
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,319
when it comes to seniority and skill,

165
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:17,600
who can hold a candle to you?

166
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,800
Exactly.

167
00:07:18,959 --> 00:07:20,240
Here, have some tea first.

168
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:24,680
No tea.

169
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,120
Let's drink.

170
00:07:30,839 --> 00:07:32,360
He cares about you.

171
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,000
He swallowed his pride to apologize.

172
00:07:35,519 --> 00:07:36,519
He's treated you well.

173
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:38,279
Treated me well? How?

174
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:39,879
Look at this!

175
00:07:40,439 --> 00:07:42,399
His daughter scratched me up!

176
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,279
This little scratch of yours,

177
00:07:43,279 --> 00:07:44,399
if you wait any longer, it'll heal on its own!

178
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:45,759
What are you talking about?

179
00:07:46,519 --> 00:07:47,639
He didn't lay a finger on you.

180
00:07:47,639 --> 00:07:48,800
It wasn't him who hit you.

181
00:07:49,319 --> 00:07:50,600
You want him to hit me, too?

182
00:07:50,959 --> 00:07:51,279
No, that's not it.

183
00:07:51,279 --> 00:07:52,759
Qianjin, listen to me.

184
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:53,920
When you're married,

185
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:55,399
you can't be so petty.

186
00:07:55,839 --> 00:07:57,040
You have to look at the big picture.

187
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:58,360
Look at Jin Jingran.

188
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,519
He has a steady job,

189
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,439
and he's generous with you.

190
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,600
That's pretty good.

191
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:05,040
Wait, Ma Laijiao, whose side are you on?

192
00:08:05,279 --> 00:08:06,680
Is this my fault now?

193
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,199
Shouldn't you be sticking up for me?

194
00:08:08,199 --> 00:08:09,000
I'm the one who got bullied!

195
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,879
Fine, fine, I'll shut up.

196
00:08:09,879 --> 00:08:10,519
Then tell me,

197
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:11,560
what are you gonna do now?

198
00:08:12,839 --> 00:08:13,240
Get a divorce.

199
00:08:14,079 --> 00:08:15,040
Worst comes to worst, I'll divorce him!

200
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:17,240
I'll go out and make my own money!

201
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:18,839
I can support myself!

202
00:08:18,839 --> 00:08:20,079
You're so capable, then go earn it!

203
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,199
Lao Ma!

204
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:28,920
For guys our age,

205
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,199
what are we most afraid of?

206
00:08:32,519 --> 00:08:33,080
What?

207
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:35,240
Women.

208
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:39,440
What are you laughing at?

209
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:41,600
Take me, for example.

210
00:08:42,519 --> 00:08:43,600
My ex-girlfriend

211
00:08:44,759 --> 00:08:45,559
went broke.

212
00:08:47,519 --> 00:08:48,279
Gotta help her out.

213
00:08:51,279 --> 00:08:51,879
Takes money.

214
00:08:52,919 --> 00:08:53,879
My wife,

215
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:56,039
gorgeous as ever.

216
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,080
Gotta provide for her.

217
00:08:59,320 --> 00:08:59,879
Takes money.

218
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:01,879
My daughter

219
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:04,919
missed ten-plus years of a father's love.

220
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,000
Gotta make it up to her.

221
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:09,720
Takes money.

222
00:09:10,919 --> 00:09:11,559
Broke.

223
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:13,360
Always broke.

224
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:14,840
You guys,

225
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:16,639
have one at most,

226
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,399
two tops.

227
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,440
Your boy here has three.

228
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,320
Tell me, aren't I incredible?

229
00:09:25,919 --> 00:09:26,399
Incredible.

230
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,200
Am I not blessed?

231
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,039
In... incredibly blessed.

232
00:09:33,879 --> 00:09:34,240
Drink.

233
00:09:41,559 --> 00:09:42,000
Old Jin!

234
00:09:43,879 --> 00:09:44,240
Old Jin!

235
00:10:05,639 --> 00:10:06,360
But look,

236
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,480
take my advice.

237
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,360
No matter how much a woman fusses,

238
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,399
she still needs someone

239
00:10:10,399 --> 00:10:11,720
caring and attentive by her side.

240
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:13,399
Someone to share sweet words with,

241
00:10:13,399 --> 00:10:14,720
so life actually has something to look forward to.

242
00:10:15,039 --> 00:10:17,000
Otherwise, what kind of life are you living?

243
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:18,720
All you talk about is making money.

244
00:10:18,879 --> 00:10:19,639
No matter how much you make,

245
00:10:19,639 --> 00:10:20,759
are you going to sleep with cash every night?

246
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,320
If I could meet someone like that,

247
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,080
as long as he didn't hit me,

248
00:10:25,399 --> 00:10:26,600
he wouldn't even need to make money.

249
00:10:27,039 --> 00:10:28,200
Even if he got drunk and acted up,

250
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,200
as long as he still thought of me,

251
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,440
I'd scrape by on scraps with him,

252
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,039
and be glad to do it.

253
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,639
Jin Jingran treats you so well.

254
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:36,919
You're acting weird.

255
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:38,879
How am I acting weird?

256
00:10:39,559 --> 00:10:40,799
Everything about you is off.

257
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:43,000
What did I even do that's so weird?

258
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,279
Are you seeing someone?

259
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:48,399
No, I'm not.

260
00:10:48,639 --> 00:10:49,679
You definitely are. Spill it! Who?

261
00:10:49,679 --> 00:10:50,879
No, I'm not dating anyone.

262
00:10:50,879 --> 00:10:51,600
I can tell.

263
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,600
As if I don't know you.

264
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,360
Dating?

265
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,159
Who would I be dating?

266
00:10:54,159 --> 00:10:54,840
The stove?

267
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:55,639
Come on,

268
00:10:56,399 --> 00:10:56,960
who is it really?

269
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:57,960
Do I know him?

270
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,399
Even if I were, I wouldn't tell you.

271
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,720
Hey, we were talking about you.

272
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:03,120
How much longer are you staying at your dad's?

273
00:11:06,279 --> 00:11:07,360
I don't know either.

274
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:10,039
You all say I can rely on my dad,

275
00:11:10,639 --> 00:11:12,159
but look at the state he's in now.

276
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,399
Not only can't I help out,

277
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,840
I still have to depend on him to feed me.

278
00:11:18,159 --> 00:11:19,919
I'm pushing thirty,

279
00:11:19,919 --> 00:11:22,399
and I'm living worse than a good-for-nothing.

280
00:11:22,399 --> 00:11:23,919
Don't talk about yourself like that.

281
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:25,639
You're so pretty,

282
00:11:25,879 --> 00:11:26,960
your dad loves you so much,

283
00:11:29,679 --> 00:11:30,480
and your older brother

284
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:31,720
spoils you rotten.

285
00:11:32,159 --> 00:11:32,879
You're so lucky.

286
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:33,840
See?

287
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:36,720
Even you can't name any other strengths of mine.

288
00:11:36,879 --> 00:11:37,600
Aside from being pretty,

289
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,720
I have nothing going for me.

290
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,919
I'm just a pretty face.

291
00:11:39,919 --> 00:11:41,039
That's not what I meant.

292
00:11:41,039 --> 00:11:42,639
That's exactly what you meant.

293
00:11:42,639 --> 00:11:43,399
Let me tell you,

294
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,919
I'm going to prove to all of you

295
00:11:45,919 --> 00:11:47,039
that I'm not just a pretty face!

296
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,480
I've already sent out several resumes.

297
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,480
Someone will definitely hire me.

298
00:11:49,759 --> 00:11:51,039
I'll... I'll get a job out there.

299
00:11:51,039 --> 00:11:51,919
I'll make big money,

300
00:11:52,039 --> 00:11:53,639
and I'll prove it to every single one of you!

301
00:11:53,639 --> 00:11:54,240
Fine, fine, go ahead.

302
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,639
I won't let you look down on me!

303
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,000
Best of luck to you.

304
00:12:03,679 --> 00:12:05,360
Ma Laijiao, let me warn you.

305
00:12:05,679 --> 00:12:06,799
You've already been burned once.

306
00:12:06,919 --> 00:12:08,519
I don't care who you're dating,

307
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,559
just remember one thing:

308
00:12:09,879 --> 00:12:10,799
if a man could be trusted,

309
00:12:10,799 --> 00:12:12,279
pigs could fly.

310
00:12:12,679 --> 00:12:13,559
Got it?

311
00:12:21,639 --> 00:12:22,279
Lao San,

312
00:12:24,559 --> 00:12:26,279
tell Dad the truth.

313
00:12:27,399 --> 00:12:28,759
Your two older brothers,

314
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,480
what's really going on with them?

315
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:35,480
Old man,

316
00:12:36,679 --> 00:12:37,720
I won't hide it from you.

317
00:12:38,679 --> 00:12:40,279
The older two had a fight

318
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,399
at the construction site.

319
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,639
They even dragged me in as a witness.

320
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:46,000
But I think,

321
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:47,639
even though they fought,

322
00:12:48,039 --> 00:12:49,360
they talked things out,

323
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,639
which is actually good.

324
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:58,399
Lao San,

325
00:12:59,679 --> 00:13:01,039
your two older brothers,

326
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,600
you might not share the same mother,

327
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,799
but you're still brothers by blood.

328
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,159
In the future,

329
00:13:13,799 --> 00:13:15,399
if you ever run into trouble,

330
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,399
they won't leave you hanging.

331
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:21,279
Your little sister is your full sister,

332
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,399
from the same mother.

333
00:13:25,879 --> 00:13:28,200
She's my only precious daughter.

334
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,960
Take good care of her for me.

335
00:13:34,039 --> 00:13:34,519
Okay.

336
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:35,879
Got it.

337
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,120
When you have time,

338
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:40,240
take your sister

339
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,279
to visit your mother's grave.

340
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:51,200
All her life,

341
00:13:52,639 --> 00:13:53,919
she had it so hard.

342
00:13:55,519 --> 00:13:56,720
At such a young age,

343
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,759
she married me.

344
00:13:59,559 --> 00:14:00,799
Right after marrying in,

345
00:14:01,919 --> 00:14:03,159
she became a stepmother,

346
00:14:05,639 --> 00:14:07,279
raising your two older brothers.

347
00:14:08,879 --> 00:14:10,200
For this family,

348
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:13,159
she endured so much hardship.

349
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:18,919
Take your sister,

350
00:14:20,639 --> 00:14:21,720
and go visit your mother.

351
00:14:24,759 --> 00:14:25,840
Burn some paper money,

352
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,039
talk to her for a bit,

353
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:31,200
tell her to be well on the other side,

354
00:14:32,519 --> 00:14:33,240
and wait for me.

355
00:15:19,679 --> 00:15:21,799
Brother Xiuming went in completely alone.

356
00:15:21,919 --> 00:15:22,879
Not a single one dared to move.

357
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:23,879
He intimidated every last one of them.

358
00:15:23,879 --> 00:15:24,399
Really?

359
00:15:24,639 --> 00:15:25,559
You know what that was like?

360
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:28,799
God of War Zhao Zilong, charging in and out seven times!

361
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,519
Brother Xiuming, you're incredible!

362
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,200
Impressive, seriously!

363
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,279
Brother Xiuming, Brother Xiuming, awesome!

364
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,000
Brother Xiuming!

365
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:34,399
Awesome!

366
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:34,960
Amazing!

367
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:35,720
Impressive!

368
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:36,759
Go on, get back to work.

369
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:37,279
Back to work.

370
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,519
Qiangzi, come here.

371
00:15:39,039 --> 00:15:39,519
That was amazing!

372
00:15:39,519 --> 00:15:40,240
Get to work, get to work.

373
00:15:40,759 --> 00:15:42,519
Wait, what's going on here?

374
00:15:42,879 --> 00:15:44,480
What you did at the Ma site last night...

375
00:15:44,639 --> 00:15:45,480
...all the guys heard about it.

376
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,840
You made quite a splash!

377
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:47,679
It was nothing.

378
00:15:47,879 --> 00:15:48,519
Impressive!

379
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:49,919
You useless coward!

380
00:15:49,919 --> 00:15:51,000
Dumping the cargo out in the open!

381
00:15:51,279 --> 00:15:52,519
Tomorrow we'll have to hire people to drag it inside!

382
00:15:52,639 --> 00:15:53,360
There was no room to unload!

383
00:15:53,799 --> 00:15:54,720
You're blaming that on me?

384
00:15:54,759 --> 00:15:55,720
Let me tell you, watch your attitude with me!

385
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,360
What's going on here?

386
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:57,759
No idea.

387
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:58,960
Let's check it out.

388
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,399
Let me see, let me look.

389
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:01,720
I'm telling you...

390
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,600
...I didn't do this for free!

391
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,360
Brother Mingming.

392
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:04,960
Uh...

393
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,080
Well...

394
00:16:06,159 --> 00:16:06,759
Perfect timing!

395
00:16:07,039 --> 00:16:07,919
Whose truck is this?

396
00:16:08,919 --> 00:16:10,000
Changfu's, probably.

397
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
The driver is throwing a fit again.

398
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,440
Look at Changfu's bunch...

399
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:13,960
...skimming my dad's profits...

400
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:14,840
...for how many years now?

401
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:17,519
My dad isn't tough like me.

402
00:16:18,039 --> 00:16:19,039
If we had our own trucks...

403
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:19,480
...right?

404
00:16:19,759 --> 00:16:20,799
...we wouldn't have to let...

405
00:16:21,039 --> 00:16:22,200
...Changfu's guys push us around every day.

406
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,000
Always walking on eggshells.

407
00:16:24,799 --> 00:16:25,279
Exactly.

408
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:26,720
Speaking of this...

409
00:16:27,279 --> 00:16:27,840
...why don't we just...

410
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:30,080
...buy some new equipment...

411
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,360
...and expand our operations?

412
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:33,879
Then you have to explain it clearly to Uncle.

413
00:16:33,879 --> 00:16:35,200
We can get it done either way!

414
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,200
Why—why talk to my dad?

415
00:16:37,759 --> 00:16:38,600
For something this small...

416
00:16:39,279 --> 00:16:40,279
...can't the two of us call the shots?

417
00:16:41,159 --> 00:16:41,799
We can, we can.

418
00:16:42,039 --> 00:16:42,399
Fine, fine.

419
00:16:42,559 --> 00:16:43,120
Are you done?

420
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,159
Sister-in-law is waiting for you.

421
00:16:45,279 --> 00:16:45,679
Coming!

422
00:16:46,559 --> 00:16:47,919
S-Sister-in-law...

423
00:16:49,639 --> 00:16:50,320
Go on, hurry.

424
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:54,840
Yesterday...

425
00:16:55,279 --> 00:16:56,279
...what happened at the Ma site...

426
00:16:56,279 --> 00:16:57,200
...did you hear about it?

427
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,200
I know.

428
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,559
You almost scared my dad to death!

429
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:00,840
I'm sorry.

430
00:17:01,279 --> 00:17:01,720
But do you know...

431
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:02,759
...where I slept last night?

432
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,519
Why am I even telling you this?

433
00:17:04,519 --> 00:17:05,759
I slept at their construction site all night.

434
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,640
What's that supposed to mean?

435
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:17,759
What are you doing?

436
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,039
I'm fine.

437
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:19,839
Go in where?

438
00:17:26,079 --> 00:17:26,720
Jia, Jia!

439
00:17:41,599 --> 00:17:42,599
I... I, um...

440
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,680
I got carried away last night.

441
00:17:49,079 --> 00:17:50,559
Please don't cry.

442
00:17:51,759 --> 00:17:52,200
Jiayin.

443
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:04,640
Slept in until now, huh?

444
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:05,640
Quite capable, aren't you?

445
00:18:07,119 --> 00:18:08,119
Feeling proud of yourself, are you?

446
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:09,799
Riding high, aren't you?

447
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,559
Did I go too easy on you?

448
00:18:12,559 --> 00:18:13,200
Sai Xiuming!

449
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,240
What were you thinking?

450
00:18:15,519 --> 00:18:16,759
You pinned him down in the rain and beat him!

451
00:18:16,759 --> 00:18:17,799
What on earth were you thinking?

452
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,079
What did Ma Laibu even do?

453
00:18:20,319 --> 00:18:21,720
You were on the Ma family's construction site,

454
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:24,119
and a Sai beat up a Ma!

455
00:18:24,319 --> 00:18:25,400
Do you have any brains at all?

456
00:18:28,799 --> 00:18:29,200
Stop right there!

457
00:18:29,559 --> 00:18:30,119
I'm not done talking to you!

458
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,319
Where did you sleep last night?

459
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,359
Brother Ming slept at the Ma site.

460
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,799
The Ma site is such a mess, right?

461
00:18:42,039 --> 00:18:43,119
They couldn't hold it down without him.

462
00:18:47,119 --> 00:18:48,000
Didn't you get into a fight?

463
00:18:48,599 --> 00:18:49,599
Your clothes aren't even dirty.

464
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:50,720
Took them off before fighting.

465
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:51,839
No, w-well...

466
00:18:52,279 --> 00:18:54,119
Didn't... didn't he get them cleaned?

467
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:54,839
Wow, nice.

468
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:56,480
All grown up now.

469
00:18:57,519 --> 00:18:57,839
No.

470
00:18:57,839 --> 00:18:58,680
Washing your own clothes now.

471
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,160
Well, Ma... Ma Laijiao...

472
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:02,279
I knew it.

473
00:19:05,559 --> 00:19:06,200
Then the clothes I brought you,

474
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,000
are you changing or not?

475
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:11,319
I'll change.

476
00:19:11,599 --> 00:19:12,400
Then take them off, quick.

477
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,480
I'll take them back and wash them properly.

478
00:19:15,799 --> 00:19:16,759
Fine, fine, I'll change.

479
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:25,000
This ledger...

480
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,319
You brought the ledger back.

481
00:19:27,519 --> 00:19:28,599
What's the point of bringing it back?

482
00:19:31,319 --> 00:19:32,359
There's no money in the account.

483
00:19:32,759 --> 00:19:34,079
We can't even pay the workers' wages.

484
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,279
It's a hot potato.

485
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,359
We can't even get rid of it.

486
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:38,119
Did you know about this?

487
00:19:40,799 --> 00:19:42,279
Look, don't... don't panic yet.

488
00:19:42,599 --> 00:19:43,559
Look at the workers outside,

489
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:44,920
aren't they all still working?

490
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:46,920
Once the Phase Three funds come in,

491
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,240
it'll ease our pressure a lot.

492
00:19:48,359 --> 00:19:49,160
Everything will be sorted out.

493
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:50,799
Come on, come in.

494
00:19:50,799 --> 00:19:51,480
Please, come inside.

495
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,200
Old Wang.

496
00:19:52,599 --> 00:19:53,200
What are you doing?

497
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:54,759
No, no.

498
00:19:54,759 --> 00:19:55,680
You can just say it right here.

499
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:56,920
You owe us a week's wages.

500
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:57,720
When are you paying us?

501
00:19:58,039 --> 00:19:58,359
Look...

502
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,359
You... all of you,

503
00:20:00,519 --> 00:20:01,039
wait a couple of days.

504
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,640
When has the Sai family ever owed you money?

505
00:20:02,759 --> 00:20:04,160
We can't even put food on the table!

506
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:04,960
Look at this...

507
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,599
If you don't want to work, leave.

508
00:20:06,839 --> 00:20:08,039
Don't say that, don't say that.

509
00:20:08,039 --> 00:20:08,720
Come on, Old Wang.

510
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:09,359
When has our Sai family

511
00:20:09,359 --> 00:20:10,400
ever owed you any money?

512
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:11,680
It's not a big deal.

513
00:20:11,839 --> 00:20:12,680
Come to my office, let's talk one-on-one.

514
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:13,799
Give us two days, just two days.

515
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:20,839
Xi'zi.

516
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,039
Look at you, you finally got yours too, huh?

517
00:20:24,759 --> 00:20:26,640
Neither of us got away clean.

518
00:20:29,839 --> 00:20:30,880
Used to piss standing up,

519
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:31,960
now you're pissing lying down.

520
00:20:32,519 --> 00:20:33,519
Look at you, putting on airs.

521
00:20:34,559 --> 00:20:35,039
I say,

522
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:36,559
he can't keep up.

523
00:20:37,039 --> 00:20:38,240
Doesn't have as much as mine.

524
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:38,920
Right?

525
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:41,759
You're competing over that too?

526
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,160
Damn right.

527
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:46,039
These two damn things are way too heavy.

528
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,759
I won't hold them for you anymore.

529
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:49,680
Keep them safe yourself.

530
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:50,559
Fine, fine, I'll take them.

531
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:54,160
See this worthless life of mine?

532
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,599
Even the King of Hell didn't want it.

533
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:58,400
So what about our three-way partnership?

534
00:20:58,880 --> 00:20:59,839
Shouldn't we get it moving?

535
00:20:59,839 --> 00:21:00,839
Yeah, yeah, let's get it going.

536
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,640
To tell you the truth,

537
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:03,960
without both of you around,

538
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:05,079
I'd really feel lost.

539
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:13,839
Lao Ma,

540
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:15,079
what do you

541
00:21:15,279 --> 00:21:15,839
mean by this?

542
00:21:20,559 --> 00:21:21,079
Xi-zi,

543
00:21:22,359 --> 00:21:23,640
you just had surgery.

544
00:21:24,559 --> 00:21:25,279
I really shouldn't

545
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,319
be telling you this,

546
00:21:28,039 --> 00:21:28,559
but

547
00:21:28,759 --> 00:21:30,079
things on-site are just too tough.

548
00:21:30,839 --> 00:21:32,839
The Phase 3 funds still haven't come through.

549
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,839
I... I really can't take it anymore.

550
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,079
Your second son

551
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,599
is capable and full of ideas,

552
00:21:41,279 --> 00:21:41,880
but right now,

553
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:44,079
he's not on the same page as you.

554
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:45,240
He even urged me

555
00:21:45,559 --> 00:21:46,799
to pull out early,

556
00:21:47,359 --> 00:21:48,240
take my money, and walk away.

557
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,000
Even if the three of us partner up,

558
00:21:51,359 --> 00:21:53,519
who can we count on down the road?

559
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:57,359
As for this matter,

560
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,119
you can't really blame Xiuliang.

561
00:21:59,200 --> 00:21:59,559
Right?

562
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:02,440
His law firm

563
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,880
took on Tengyue's legal business,

564
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,319
so now he's Shi Yongnian's man.

565
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:08,079
Shi Yongnian is digging his heels in.

566
00:22:08,319 --> 00:22:09,079
If you two don't back out,

567
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:10,799
he won't release the Phase 3 funds.

568
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,839
That leaves me and Xiuliang caught in the middle.

569
00:22:13,319 --> 00:22:14,440
When you get a chance,

570
00:22:15,039 --> 00:22:16,920
you need to talk things through with Xiuliang.

571
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:23,799
All these years,

572
00:22:25,559 --> 00:22:27,079
you two brothers helped me along

573
00:22:28,039 --> 00:22:29,119
so we could make money together,

574
00:22:30,839 --> 00:22:32,240
and you never treated me wrong.

575
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:33,440
Truth be told,

576
00:22:34,039 --> 00:22:35,519
the three of us partnering up

577
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:36,799
was just

578
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,359
your way of looking out for me.

579
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:39,640
But look at me,

580
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,720
the way I am now:

581
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:43,319
my money's split,

582
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,279
my family's torn apart,

583
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:47,680
and I'm completely broken.

584
00:22:48,599 --> 00:22:49,039
As for me,

585
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:50,359
I can't put up money,

586
00:22:50,559 --> 00:22:51,559
I can't put in labor,

587
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:53,240
and I can't bring in workers.

588
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:55,319
I'm just a huge burden.

589
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:56,960
For this project,

590
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,119
you two brothers should just do it.

591
00:23:01,599 --> 00:23:02,200
Dacheng,

592
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:05,319
the three of us swore an oath together.

593
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,160
We gave our word

594
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:07,319
that no one gets left behind, right?

595
00:23:07,319 --> 00:23:07,759
I know,

596
00:23:07,759 --> 00:23:09,240
but it's not that you're leaving me behind.

597
00:23:09,519 --> 00:23:10,960
I just can't keep up. I...

598
00:23:11,319 --> 00:23:12,920
I just don't have the fight left in me.

599
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:18,759
Lao Wei,

600
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:20,960
where do you stand?

601
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:22,400
Xi-zi, don't worry.

602
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:22,920
I'm not backing out.

603
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:24,279
Think about it, the three of us,

604
00:23:24,279 --> 00:23:24,880
all these years,

605
00:23:25,279 --> 00:23:26,359
we've made it through so many hurdles.

606
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:26,880
Haven't we?

607
00:23:27,119 --> 00:23:27,519
Xi-zi,

608
00:23:28,279 --> 00:23:29,680
as long as you're still breathing,

609
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:30,920
I'll keep fighting alongside you.

610
00:23:32,079 --> 00:23:32,440
Good.

611
00:23:33,079 --> 00:23:33,440
Good.

612
00:23:50,759 --> 00:23:52,440
Dad, why didn't you answer your phone?

613
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:53,559
You just sent a text

614
00:23:53,559 --> 00:23:54,319
saying it's urgent,

615
00:23:54,319 --> 00:23:55,240
and then wouldn't pick up!

616
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,559
I had no idea what happened.

617
00:23:56,559 --> 00:23:57,519
You worried me to death!

618
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:06,200
Who came to see you?

619
00:24:16,279 --> 00:24:17,039
I'll change your urine bag.

620
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:20,440
How long have you two

621
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:22,400
been tied together?

622
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,359
Two boxes for Uncle Wei,

623
00:24:36,759 --> 00:24:37,799
and two for Uncle Ma, right?

624
00:24:44,519 --> 00:24:45,200
Go ahead.

625
00:24:46,039 --> 00:24:46,880
With Tengyue,

626
00:24:48,079 --> 00:24:48,519
wasn't it just

627
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,200
the day the firm opened,

628
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:53,119
the day of my surgery?

629
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,839
It hasn't been long.

630
00:24:58,200 --> 00:24:59,680
You can still pull out.

631
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,160
How can I pull out?

632
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,039
We already signed a contract!

633
00:25:04,559 --> 00:25:05,720
Besides, Tengyue...

634
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:07,640
every law firm is eyeing that juicy prize!

635
00:25:08,119 --> 00:25:09,079
Can I... can I just pull out?

636
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:09,920
I can't.

637
00:25:15,759 --> 00:25:16,039
Dad,

638
00:25:18,359 --> 00:25:19,720
do you and Shi Yongnian

639
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:20,720
have some bad blood?

640
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:22,400
If there's something,

641
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:23,640
just tell me.

642
00:25:23,799 --> 00:25:25,759
Look at him insisting on kicking us out,

643
00:25:26,039 --> 00:25:27,200
and now you want me to pull out.

644
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:28,440
Something's definitely up.

645
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:29,400
Just tell me.

646
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,359
Fine, fine.

647
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:38,079
If you won't say,

648
00:25:38,079 --> 00:25:38,799
I won't ask.

649
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:40,559
Whatever happened between you two

650
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:42,079
has nothing to do with me.

651
00:25:42,079 --> 00:25:42,680
On our end, this is

652
00:25:43,079 --> 00:25:43,880
a corporate partnership.

653
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:44,519
They're two completely different things.

654
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:49,319
Go talk to your Uncle Wei as soon as possible.

655
00:25:49,559 --> 00:25:51,319
Ask him how much I should put in.

656
00:25:51,799 --> 00:25:52,759
On one condition:

657
00:25:53,039 --> 00:25:53,599
I

658
00:25:53,839 --> 00:25:55,160
must have the majority stake.

659
00:25:55,599 --> 00:25:56,680
Have him name a price.

660
00:25:57,599 --> 00:25:59,400
Wait, Uncle Ma already backed out.

661
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,319
Why are you still hung up on the merger?

662
00:26:01,319 --> 00:26:02,400
No matter who backs out,

663
00:26:03,039 --> 00:26:04,039
I'm still doing it.

664
00:26:04,440 --> 00:26:05,880
I have to give this family

665
00:26:06,279 --> 00:26:07,559
a fallback plan.

666
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:10,680
I have to expand the construction team.

667
00:26:11,119 --> 00:26:11,839
You

668
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:14,920
need to think of this family too.

669
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,880
If the construction team goes under,

670
00:26:17,119 --> 00:26:17,920
your older brother

671
00:26:18,799 --> 00:26:20,240
and your younger siblings...

672
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,559
what will happen to them?

673
00:26:22,039 --> 00:26:23,680
They're not as capable as you.

674
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:26,000
You have to help them.

675
00:26:26,519 --> 00:26:28,119
Help this family.

676
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:43,880
Leaving just like that?

677
00:26:50,759 --> 00:26:51,400
I'll try.

678
00:26:51,759 --> 00:26:53,440
What do you mean, 'try'?

679
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,160
You have to.

680
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:59,440
In this whole world,

681
00:27:00,799 --> 00:27:02,799
your own father in that hospital bed

682
00:27:02,799 --> 00:27:04,240
is the one you can't let down.

683
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,039
Caught in the middle? You just have to take it.

684
00:27:09,359 --> 00:27:10,680
And your dad's stubbornness,

685
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,480
you just have to put up with that, too.

686
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:26,680
You're unbelievable.

687
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:28,039
Every time we view an apartment, it's at night.

688
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:29,680
I can't even see what the outside looks like.

689
00:27:30,039 --> 00:27:30,519
Don't worry.

690
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:31,759
The surroundings and amenities outside—

691
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:32,559
I've already checked them all out for you.

692
00:27:32,839 --> 00:27:33,720
You just need to look inside.

693
00:27:34,440 --> 00:27:34,759
Come on.

694
00:27:35,119 --> 00:27:35,559
I'll take you in.

695
00:27:39,480 --> 00:27:40,279
Come on, let's head in.

696
00:27:43,759 --> 00:27:44,359
Take a look around.

697
00:27:45,039 --> 00:27:47,000
Two-bedroom, newly renovated, brand new.

698
00:27:47,799 --> 00:27:48,960
You can't see much outside at night,

699
00:27:49,119 --> 00:27:50,319
but the view during the day is amazing.

700
00:27:50,799 --> 00:27:52,039
It's close to where you work,

701
00:27:52,039 --> 00:27:53,160
and not far from Uncle Ma's place, either.

702
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,920
It's just slightly pricier than that one-bedroom.

703
00:27:56,119 --> 00:27:56,960
But the way I see it,

704
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:59,119
you'll get married and have kids sooner or later.

705
00:27:59,279 --> 00:28:00,480
Might as well get it all sorted in one go.

706
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,759
Save where you should, spend where you must.

707
00:28:02,039 --> 00:28:03,240
You sure think far ahead.

708
00:28:04,359 --> 00:28:05,839
But this place really is pretty nice.

709
00:28:06,279 --> 00:28:07,160
Why are they selling it?

710
00:28:07,319 --> 00:28:09,599
A young couple prepared it as their marital home.

711
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:10,960
Look at the floors.

712
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:11,880
Look at the furniture.

713
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:12,880
All carefully picked out.

714
00:28:13,319 --> 00:28:14,240
Right after they finished renovating,

715
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:14,920
they broke up.

716
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:15,759
Now they're desperate to sell.

717
00:28:16,119 --> 00:28:18,079
So now's the perfect time to buy.

718
00:28:18,599 --> 00:28:20,160
After putting in so much effort

719
00:28:20,319 --> 00:28:21,400
and spending all that money,

720
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:22,480
someone else ends up getting a bargain.

721
00:28:24,799 --> 00:28:25,599
Exactly.

722
00:28:27,799 --> 00:28:28,559
So,

723
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,240
to not let their efforts go to waste,

724
00:28:32,119 --> 00:28:34,000
I think you should find someone,

725
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:36,200
become a couple,

726
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:39,559
and put this marital home to good use.

727
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:41,160
What do you think?

728
00:28:46,839 --> 00:28:47,200
Fine.

729
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,599
I'll take this place.

730
00:28:50,359 --> 00:28:51,440
Tomorrow I'll sort out the paperwork,

731
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,440
and the day after, I'll find a partner.

732
00:28:53,759 --> 00:28:54,640
All in one go.

733
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,160
Hey, come on.

734
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:59,640
I'm doing you such a huge favor,

735
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:00,440
and you won't even let me

736
00:29:00,799 --> 00:29:02,200
poke a little harmless fun?

737
00:29:07,279 --> 00:29:08,759
Well, since you helped me out so much,

738
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:10,519
what reward do you want?

739
00:29:16,279 --> 00:29:17,559
What reward could I possibly want?

740
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:21,279
How about this?

741
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:22,279
I'll treat you to dinner.

742
00:29:22,759 --> 00:29:23,440
Pick anywhere you like.

743
00:29:26,799 --> 00:29:27,359
Or,

744
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:28,960
I'll give you a nice red packet.

745
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:31,720
But as for the loan, forget it.

746
00:29:32,079 --> 00:29:32,400
Why, you...

747
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:46,960
Is this reward

748
00:29:48,319 --> 00:29:48,839
good enough?

749
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:56,559
Can you make it any cheaper?

750
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:01,960
Sure.

751
00:30:18,119 --> 00:30:18,720
Jiaqi.

752
00:30:19,759 --> 00:30:20,319
Jiaqi!

753
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:42,519
What are you doing here?

754
00:30:43,559 --> 00:30:44,000
Nothing.

755
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:47,960
Dinner's ready.

756
00:30:49,559 --> 00:30:49,960
Okay.

757
00:30:56,799 --> 00:30:57,759
Why'd you stop playing?

758
00:30:59,559 --> 00:31:00,039
Boring.

759
00:31:02,559 --> 00:31:03,720
It's no fun anymore.

760
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:06,359
Alright.

761
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:09,799
So...

762
00:31:14,519 --> 00:31:16,039
is your wife coming back?

763
00:31:18,279 --> 00:31:19,519
Do you want her to come back?

764
00:31:20,359 --> 00:31:22,680
She took all the clothes I wanted to wear.

765
00:31:24,079 --> 00:31:25,240
Of course I want her back.

766
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:33,720
What do you want me to do?

767
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:35,440
Say I'm sorry?

768
00:31:36,680 --> 00:31:37,440
That's easy enough.

769
00:31:39,359 --> 00:31:40,359
I can go say it.

770
00:31:43,759 --> 00:31:44,440
You...

771
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,319
just don't cause any trouble.

772
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:51,400
What?

773
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:54,839
Nothing.

774
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:05,359
Dad,

775
00:32:10,039 --> 00:32:11,079
I'm homesick.

776
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:15,680
I miss my mom,

777
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:17,039
my friends,

778
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,720
even the awful cafeteria food.

779
00:32:22,119 --> 00:32:23,160
When can I go back?

780
00:32:26,519 --> 00:32:27,039
I know.

781
00:32:29,559 --> 00:32:29,960
I know.

782
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:36,079
I talked to your mom.

783
00:32:37,559 --> 00:32:38,440
I promise

784
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:42,960
I'll get you back as soon as I can.

785
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:45,319
Okay?

786
00:32:47,039 --> 00:32:48,720
Have I been a lot of trouble?

787
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:49,640
No.

788
00:32:53,559 --> 00:32:54,759
Don't worry about that.

789
00:32:55,799 --> 00:32:56,759
Having you here...

790
00:32:58,000 --> 00:32:58,519
is really nice.

791
00:34:00,519 --> 00:34:00,960
Sister-in-law.

792
00:34:03,119 --> 00:34:04,200
Thinking about your wife?

793
00:34:06,240 --> 00:34:06,680
Um...

794
00:34:08,039 --> 00:34:08,639
She's home, right?

795
00:34:09,079 --> 00:34:09,400
She is.

796
00:34:11,199 --> 00:34:12,000
This is for Zhenzhu.

797
00:34:12,079 --> 00:34:12,639
She loves this.

798
00:34:13,599 --> 00:34:14,320
This is for you.

799
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:15,559
Taking care of the whole family...

800
00:34:15,559 --> 00:34:16,039
...thanks for all your hard work.

801
00:34:31,079 --> 00:34:31,559
Qianjin,

802
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:35,679
can you open the door, please?

803
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:37,079
Qianjin.

804
00:34:38,559 --> 00:34:39,199
When you're not home,

805
00:34:39,199 --> 00:34:40,360
my life just feels...

806
00:34:40,440 --> 00:34:41,440
so dull and empty.

807
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:43,360
I really mean it.

808
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:47,360
Qianjin,

809
00:34:47,840 --> 00:34:49,360
let's not stoop to a kid's level,

810
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:49,880
all right?

811
00:34:50,039 --> 00:34:51,119
She's just a child.

812
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:52,800
She grew up overseas.

813
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,920
Plus, Jiaqi grew up without a father's love.

814
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:56,599
She doesn't know any manners.

815
00:34:58,639 --> 00:34:59,079
Qianjin,

816
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,199
think about Dad.

817
00:35:01,480 --> 00:35:02,199
Dad's health is bad,

818
00:35:02,199 --> 00:35:02,880
and he's still sick.

819
00:35:03,079 --> 00:35:03,840
This little conflict of ours,

820
00:35:04,119 --> 00:35:05,039
let's not let him find out.

821
00:35:08,719 --> 00:35:09,920
Sister-in-law is right out here.

822
00:35:10,639 --> 00:35:11,440
Let me come in so we can talk,

823
00:35:11,440 --> 00:35:12,039
okay?

824
00:35:12,559 --> 00:35:13,800
Should I give you two some space?

825
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:14,480
No, that's not it...

826
00:35:16,159 --> 00:35:16,639
Qianjin...

827
00:35:31,159 --> 00:35:31,960
Don't be mad anymore.

828
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:33,760
It's my fault.

829
00:35:34,480 --> 00:35:35,320
I didn't handle things well.

830
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:37,960
I'll work hard to make money.

831
00:35:38,639 --> 00:35:39,199
As soon as I have money,

832
00:35:39,199 --> 00:35:39,920
the first thing I'll do

833
00:35:40,679 --> 00:35:41,719
is send Jiaqi back.

834
00:35:42,159 --> 00:35:43,559
Then it'll just be the two of us.

835
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:46,039
When you're not home,

836
00:35:47,199 --> 00:35:47,840
this place of mine

837
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:49,800
isn't really a home.

838
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:55,280
Don't cry.

839
00:35:56,119 --> 00:35:56,599
Please don't cry.

840
00:36:02,719 --> 00:36:03,280
This money...

841
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:04,639
Dad gave it to us

842
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:06,679
for emergencies.

843
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:08,400
Now that

844
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,119
his surgery went well,

845
00:36:11,480 --> 00:36:12,599
you should give it back to him.

846
00:36:26,239 --> 00:36:27,519
I didn't even make director.

847
00:36:28,639 --> 00:36:29,360
Get up.

848
00:36:40,039 --> 00:36:40,519
Well...

849
00:36:41,559 --> 00:36:42,079
Did Dad

850
00:36:42,960 --> 00:36:44,079
ever mention to you

851
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:46,320
that from the demolition payout,

852
00:36:47,159 --> 00:36:48,280
he set aside a share just for you?

853
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:51,519
What are you getting at?

854
00:36:52,480 --> 00:36:52,880
Look...

855
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:56,760
You see,

856
00:36:58,199 --> 00:36:59,320
my original plan was

857
00:36:59,639 --> 00:37:00,599
once I made enough money,

858
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:01,960
I'd send Jiaqi back.

859
00:37:03,159 --> 00:37:04,000
But right now,

860
00:37:05,039 --> 00:37:05,440
well...

861
00:37:06,079 --> 00:37:07,280
things are a bit tough,

862
00:37:08,119 --> 00:37:08,920
and money is tight.

863
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:09,719
You see...

864
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:11,519
Hear me out, okay?

865
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:13,360
Could we take a bit

866
00:37:13,679 --> 00:37:14,920
from the demolition payout for now?

867
00:37:15,159 --> 00:37:16,400
Let me send Jiaqi abroad first,

868
00:37:16,599 --> 00:37:17,639
and later... I'll work hard to earn it back.

869
00:37:17,639 --> 00:37:18,320
Jin Jingran,

870
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:20,199
have you no shame?

871
00:37:20,199 --> 00:37:21,199
Do you think my family is that cheap?!

872
00:37:21,199 --> 00:37:21,639
No, no, no...

873
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:22,840
Marrying off a daughter wasn't enough,

874
00:37:22,840 --> 00:37:24,639
and now we have to pay to raise yours too?

875
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:26,000
Don't think just because you're a doctor

876
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:26,880
and my dad is sick right now,

877
00:37:26,880 --> 00:37:28,199
you have our family by the throat!

878
00:37:28,199 --> 00:37:29,039
My dad isn't gonna die!

879
00:37:29,039 --> 00:37:29,920
Don't you worry!

880
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:30,920
I'll write an IOU. It's a loan!

881
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:31,840
Loan, my ass!

882
00:37:31,840 --> 00:37:32,679
You miserable bastard!

883
00:37:32,679 --> 00:37:33,639
Get the hell out!

884
00:37:33,639 --> 00:37:35,480
You really think money solves everything?

885
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:37,280
No wonder your ex-girlfriend ran off!

886
00:37:37,559 --> 00:37:39,079
No wonder your daughter ignores you

887
00:37:39,079 --> 00:37:39,920
unless she's asking for money!

888
00:37:39,920 --> 00:37:41,079
Go live with your money!

889
00:37:41,079 --> 00:37:41,800
I'm just trying to talk this over...

890
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:42,639
Jingran, you should leave.

891
00:37:42,639 --> 00:37:43,760
If you stay, she won't stop yelling.

892
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:44,360
Just go.

893
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:45,920
Doctor? Ph.D.? What a load of crap!

894
00:37:46,199 --> 00:37:47,280
You're all scumbags!

895
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:49,199
All your education went straight to the dogs!

896
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:51,119
Get out! I told you to get lost, hear me?

897
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:52,360
I said leave!

898
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:53,559
Alright, that's enough! Stop it!

899
00:37:54,159 --> 00:37:55,480
I never want to see you again!

900
00:37:55,480 --> 00:37:56,920
Calm down. There are so many people around.

901
00:37:57,239 --> 00:37:58,039
There's a crowd outside.

902
00:37:59,440 --> 00:38:00,800
Wait, what's going on here?

903
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:02,440
Blowing up out of nowhere.

904
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:03,440
Weren't things fine just a minute ago?

905
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:04,280
All sweet-talking outside and everything.

906
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:05,400
Fine, my foot!

907
00:38:06,599 --> 00:38:08,800
Whenever we fight, he just tries to sweet-talk me,

908
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:10,239
or bribe me with money.

909
00:38:10,599 --> 00:38:12,119
Does he have an ounce of sincerity?

910
00:38:14,639 --> 00:38:15,880
That's already not bad.

911
00:38:16,159 --> 00:38:17,800
Your older brother can't even manage either.

912
00:38:18,119 --> 00:38:19,800
At least my brother takes responsibility!

913
00:38:20,159 --> 00:38:22,320
Jin Jingran actually wants to touch my dad's money

914
00:38:22,519 --> 00:38:24,400
to send his daughter back to the US!

915
00:38:24,679 --> 00:38:26,079
My dad is still lying there sick!

916
00:38:26,079 --> 00:38:27,840
How could I ever bring myself to ask for that?!

917
00:38:30,840 --> 00:38:32,079
Do you think I'm a total failure?

918
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:34,440
My husband... he's like this,

919
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:36,400
and I can't even find a job myself.

920
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:38,159
I've sent out dozens of resumes,

921
00:38:38,159 --> 00:38:39,559
and not a single place wants me.

922
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:40,960
They say I'm too old,

923
00:38:41,159 --> 00:38:42,280
or that my education isn't enough.

924
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:43,800
Back when Dad was at home,

925
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:45,880
I could hold my head high whenever I visited,

926
00:38:46,119 --> 00:38:47,639
not caring what anyone in the village said.

927
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:48,920
Now that Dad's not around,

928
00:38:49,679 --> 00:38:50,119
when I go back,

929
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:51,559
I feel like a stranger visiting.

930
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:52,880
And in my own home,

931
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:54,400
that father and daughter are a team.

932
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:56,199
One earns, the other spends,

933
00:38:56,199 --> 00:38:57,639
and I'm just an outsider.

934
00:38:57,639 --> 00:39:00,000
I suddenly realize I have nowhere to belong.

935
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:02,239
Why is my life so damn hard?

936
00:39:03,119 --> 00:39:04,679
Now you know how I feel, right?

937
00:39:05,199 --> 00:39:06,119
A woman...

938
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:08,119
she really needs to have her own money.

939
00:39:08,119 --> 00:39:09,159
Yeah, you do need money.

940
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:11,559
It's just so hard to make.

941
00:39:16,679 --> 00:39:17,239
Qianjin,

942
00:39:18,719 --> 00:39:19,920
do you really want to make money?

943
00:39:22,559 --> 00:39:23,199
You know,

944
00:39:23,199 --> 00:39:24,079
well, you know how

945
00:39:24,920 --> 00:39:26,719
I make wedding dresses

946
00:39:26,719 --> 00:39:27,840
and veils for people on the side?

947
00:39:27,960 --> 00:39:29,599
The owner of that bridal workshop

948
00:39:29,599 --> 00:39:31,480
has family issues and is quitting.

949
00:39:32,039 --> 00:39:34,320
She wants to transfer the shop to me.

950
00:39:34,960 --> 00:39:36,360
Now that Dad's sick,

951
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:37,559
on my own, I...

952
00:39:38,039 --> 00:39:39,079
I can't manage it all by myself.

953
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:40,920
Why don't we

954
00:39:42,119 --> 00:39:43,440
take over that shop together

955
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:44,159
and run it as partners?

956
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:45,360
It doesn't take much investment.

957
00:39:45,679 --> 00:39:47,119
30,000 to 50,000 each is plenty,

958
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,159
and we'll definitely make a profit.

959
00:39:48,159 --> 00:39:49,079
Wen Jiayin,

960
00:39:49,360 --> 00:39:51,159
hasn't Dad treated you and Big Brother well enough?

961
00:39:51,599 --> 00:39:53,039
The construction team pays you salaries,

962
00:39:53,039 --> 00:39:54,159
and covers your living expenses.

963
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:57,119
Why are you trying to do side gigs behind their backs?

964
00:39:57,239 --> 00:39:58,639
Can you even handle it?

965
00:39:58,639 --> 00:40:00,559
I can't rely on Dad for everything.

966
00:40:00,559 --> 00:40:01,920
I need to make my own living.

967
00:40:02,199 --> 00:40:02,679
Besides,

968
00:40:02,679 --> 00:40:04,199
your big brother is a hopeless case.

969
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:05,239
If something happens to the family later

970
00:40:05,239 --> 00:40:06,039
and we need money, what then?

971
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:07,000
You're just a spoiled princess

972
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:08,039
freeloading at home every day.

973
00:40:08,039 --> 00:40:08,639
What would you know?

974
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:10,079
You finally said it!

975
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:12,119
I knew all along you resented me.

976
00:40:12,119 --> 00:40:13,840
Resenting me for freeloading, right?

977
00:40:14,159 --> 00:40:14,679
Let me tell you,

978
00:40:14,679 --> 00:40:16,039
I'll definitely find a job!

979
00:40:16,360 --> 00:40:16,880
Once I find one,

980
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,679
I'm moving out.

981
00:40:17,679 --> 00:40:19,079
I won't be an eyesore around you anymore!

982
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:20,119
Are you happy now?

983
00:40:26,320 --> 00:40:27,480
Don't even think about it.

984
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:38,159
It's almost mealtime.

985
00:40:38,159 --> 00:40:39,079
Are you eating or not?

986
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:40,960
Should I save some for you?

987
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:53,599
Are you out of your mind?

988
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,480
You must be crazy!

989
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:55,079
Damn right I am!

990
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:56,119
In this family,

991
00:40:56,199 --> 00:40:57,480
I've pretended to be normal for over a decade!

992
00:40:57,760 --> 00:40:58,320
Sai Qianjin,

993
00:40:59,239 --> 00:41:01,119
stay the hell away from Ma Laijiao from now on!

994
00:41:01,440 --> 00:41:02,480
I put up with you bullying me,

995
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:03,239
but if you dare touch her,

996
00:41:03,719 --> 00:41:04,800
I'll take you down with me!

997
00:41:05,159 --> 00:41:06,159
I want to know: on this site,

998
00:41:06,159 --> 00:41:06,960
who's in charge right now?

999
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:07,360
Who calls the shots?

1000
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:08,440
Who has the final say?

1001
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:09,760
Yeah, who really has the final say?

1002
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:11,960
Call Second Brother and get him here.

1003
00:41:12,559 --> 00:41:12,880
Go on, hurry!

1004
00:41:13,199 --> 00:41:15,320
Uncle, calling Second Brother won't help now.

1005
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:16,880
Why not?

1006
00:41:17,559 --> 00:41:19,440
Second Brother already gave the ledger to Sister-in-law.
